{"kind":"assert","text":"CF-1 (ff59ca0c): the four parts, before source edits. I read the cutover source at 99ed4a7e. The platform, derive and contract packages are the same at 9b38f07e. Plan 69fed843 v2 read main 6bfb6e16. Rulings 68356c6c, 7505fa96, 710a5d76, dd318d40, 862eb586 and 080e7c84 apply. No source edit, compiler or test ran. A claim marked UNVERIFIED is one I did not check in source.\n\n## 1. Versions\n\nAt 99ed4a7e no cohort file changes from 64112e45. The cutover allocates no new version (862eb586 point 6). It changes three declaration digests in place: platform:inbox@1, 2d4fb561 to 1110d86e, and platform:destination@5 and @6, aed97f87 to 40d9aae5. The highest version of each name is in packages/platform/src/native-declarations.generated.ts.\n\n- membership@13 (generated.ts:56) to membership@14. This version takes:\n  - `revoke-key` with an own-key branch (68356c6c 2a);\n  - the act `leave` (2b);\n  - `last-admin-kept` without its check, only for proved recovery (2c);\n  - B = 4 in place of `own-agent-key-capacity` (3a);\n  - the controller's revoke of an own agent's key (3b);\n  - `remove-member` with the own-agent branch (7505fa96 point 1).\n- rules@14 (:95) to rules@15. The install proof accepts an ordinary v2 package beside a device package (710a5d76). It retains `publication-paths@1` (4a, 4b, 4e). It refuses reference fields by an explicit choice (6).\n- directory@26 (:44) to directory@27. It pins Membership 14, Rules 15 and Destination 21. It holds exclusive prefix claims, `publication-prefix-in-use` (4c). It writes the new closed marker (5a). It receives ordinary and device creations on one closed branch.\n- destination@20 (:17) to destination@21. It judges the requested path against the proved prefixes and records `publication-path-not-declared` (5b). It keeps the fixed one-hour token of Destination 19 (6).\n- register@27 (:83) to register@28. It selects and proves Directory 27. It keeps the failed-claim final state and the separate founder and