talog-vocabulary.ts, with 9 questions. Destination 19 and 20 answer some questions differently, for example `scopeReadTokenFixedHourDestination`. Correction: CF-1 adds each new pin to each question by an explicit choice and lists the choices in its note. The frozen fixture version-questions-86179b0c.json stays unchanged.\n\nS9 is carried, not stale. The failed-claim line uses `separateRecoveryMembership` and `destination4`, at failed-claim-cohort-data.ts:39–47. `ownAgentMembership` derives from `repositoryBindingMembership`. Membership 14 and Destination 21 compose both lines explicitly.\n\n## 3. Shared paths\n\nCF-1 projects these paths:\n- packages/platform/src: new cohort and data modules; membership, own-agent-membership, device-application-*, application-install*, destination, publishing-provenance, native-catalog, version-questions, version-relations, index and the generated declarations.\n- packages/derive/src/creation-context.ts, and one test.\n- packages/contract/src/catalog-vocabulary.ts.\n- packages/scope: src/publication-policy.ts and src/applications/admission.ts.\n- The CLI, client and Page selectors: cli command-install.ts and line.ts, client creation-offer.ts.\n- apps/room/page/assets.ts, regenerated.\n- Docs, and one note.\n\nWhat each lane shares with CF-1:\n- RC-1 (cbd99dcf: bytes records.ts, its test and note). No file. CF-1 adds no `RefusalReason`. A new reason would fail to compile against `REFUSAL_CLASSES`.\n- IE-1 with FG-1 (818d7545: derive item-effects.ts, fold.ts, two tests and a note). No file. Both lanes and CF-1 change kernel package derive, so each needs its own section 7 review.\n- HL-1 (scripts/test.mjs lists, one Node classify test, a note). No file is planned. After HL-1 lands, its classify test fails CF-1 for any new test file that no stage selects.\n- PG-1 (cb07b59b). UNVERIFIED, because no lane exists: one derive function and index.ts, derive test fixtures, and possibly `Grant` in contract. No file is shared if CF-1 adds no derive export. Kernel review applies to each.\n\n## 4. Heads\n\nI propose one head, cut from the cutover review head and rebased onto main after the cutover lands. It allocates the five versions once. Its commits run in this order:\n1. Write each new pin into each version question by an explicit choice, with no behavior change.\n2. Membership 14 and its witnesses: 68356c6c points 2 and 3, and 7505fa96 point 1.\n3. Rules 15 and package admission: ordinary v2, device, and `publication-paths@1`.\n4. The creation-context marker and the Directory 27 claims.\n5. Destination 21 and the host alias check in `publicationRefusal`.\n6. Register 28, the cohort, the selectors and the new default.\n7. The reader pages and the note.\n\nThe gate proves five things:\n- Each existing pin keeps its digest and behavior.\n- Each family rule has its witness.\n- The whole-family witness passes.\n- `apps/counter`, packed by `dap pack`, installs in a new room, takes one act and replays.\n- A device package still installs and runs its command.\n\nA split into Membership 14 first and then the rest adds a gate. It also leaves an unselected pin on main between the two heads. I do not recommend it unless the checker asks for a smaller review.\n\n## Questions\n\nQ1. Does dd318d40 ask CF-1 for anything that 862eb586 has not already done in place at the cutover?\nQ2. Is the v3 marker shape of S5 acceptable? I have not checked whether `readDeviceCommandGrant` and the delegate rule fit it without other derive changes.\nQ3. Does \"proved recovery\" for `last-admin-kept` mean that the signing key equals the roster's `recoveryKey`? It is UNVERIFIED that `JudgedInput` exposes the signing key that way.\nQ4. Does a new pin in contract/src/catalog-vocabulary.ts count as a kernel addition under docs/kernel.md section 7?\nQ5. Three choices have no ruling: the new cohort's `--cohort` word, whether `--host none` moves off `unpublished`, and whether the Worker `PLATFORM_CREATION_PINS` change in CF-1 or with your deployment config."}